# API envelope

Return JSON through `api_ok` / `api_error` from `gametheca/utils/api_response.py`. Do not add a `jsonify` whose top-level keys include `error`, `message`, `status`, `success`, or `ok`.

Pick `error_code` from `ERROR_CODES`. Do not invent a token at the call site. `detail` is passed to the browser as given — no secrets, tokens, raw `.env`, or filesystem paths.

HTTP `status=` is the response code. Classic JS that still reads a body `status` (or honesty `code`) needs `body_status=` / `body_code=` — passing `status='error'` binds to HTTP.

A file may never exceed its count in `scripts/api_envelope_lint.baseline.json`. `--update` only after a genuine reduction.

```python
# ❌
return jsonify({"error": "not found"}), 404

# ✅
return api_error("not found", code="not_found")

# ✅ body `status` for classic admin JS
return api_error("library_uuid is required", code="bad_request", body_status="rejected")
```
